WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.710
Donald Trump isn’t exactly known for thinking
in foreign policy details.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:10.690
My foreign policy will always put
the interests of the American people and American

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.380
security above all else.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:16.730
But recently, Trump got specific about something
important — NATO, the North Atlantic Treaty

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:18.170
Organization.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:20.910
And what he said shocked everyone.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.989
NATO is a military alliance between the U.S.,
Canada and a large chunk of Europe.

00:00:27.989 --> 00:00:31.559
It began in 1949 as a means of deterring a
Soviet attack on Western Europe.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:36.780
In Washington, the United States breaks
a 170-year-old tradition as it joins

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.920
eleven nations in the signing of the Atlantic
Defense Treaty.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.600
Basically saying, "if you attack one of us, you'll get a response from all of us."

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:48.260
NATO has since grown to include 28 countries,
including former members of the Soviet Union.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:53.240
It intervened to end the Bosnian War in 1995,
and responded to the 9/11 attacks with a decade-long

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.550
mission in Afghanistan.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.160
The alliance has helped keep the peace
in the Northern Hemisphere for more than half

00:00:58.220 --> 00:00:59.580
a century.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.060
And now, Donald Trump has threatened to destroy
the whole thing.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.860
So, Trump was in an interview with the New York Times on July 20.

00:01:05.869 --> 00:01:07.269
And Sanger asks him...

00:01:14.409 --> 00:01:15.389
Trump replies...

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:24.740
And then Trump says...

00:01:27.759 --> 00:01:31.109
Trump is probably referring to the fact that
all the NATO countries have agreed to spend

00:01:31.109 --> 00:01:34.299
2 percent of their GDP on national defense as part of the treaty.

00:01:34.299 --> 00:01:38.869
The U.S. is one of just five countries
that met that benchmark in 2016.

00:01:38.869 --> 00:01:40.959
Trump isn’t the first to call out countries
that haven’t.

00:01:40.959 --> 00:01:46.590
The majority of allies are still
not hitting that 2 percent mark....everybody

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.649
has got to step up and everybody has got to
do better.”

00:01:48.649 --> 00:01:53.119
But Trump is the first and only one to suggest
that our commitment to NATO should be contingent

00:01:53.119 --> 00:01:54.950
on those spending levels.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.180
And even his fellow Republicans are calling
him out.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:03.160
Now, I have friends that serve in parliament in places like Estonia, that every day worry about the Russians

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.440
deciding that this is the time to re-annex and to take them back.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.920
And comments like this are not only ill-informed, they're dangerous.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.580
I, mean, it's the most successful military alliance in the history of the world.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:20.060
I want to reassure our NATO allies that, should any of them be attacked, we'll be there to defend them.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:24.620
And I'm willing to chalk this up to a rookie mistake.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.200
But Trump isn’t backing down.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.390
If Mitch McConnell says that, then he's wrong.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:32.140
So all I'm saying is they have to pay.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:33.630
So why is this such a big deal?

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.720
Because of the way that NATO works.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:38.420
NATO deters attacks through something called credible commitment.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:43.320
There’s no organization that can force the
United States to go fight for Estonia, Latvia

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.320
or Lithuania.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:48.100
A country like Russia has to believe that
the United States is willing to intervene

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.980
even if it risks World War III.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:54.170
That’s why political leaders of both parties
haven’t wavered from the commitment to defend

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:55.510
the NATO alliance.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:03:00.480
And he used the NATO alliance almost as a transactional, business alliance.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.320
So that is a complete break with American policy.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:06.420
And Trump’s remarks come at a time when
NATO is particularly relevant.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.790
Russia invaded Ukraine in 2014, even annexing
part of the country.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.280
This came just six years after its invasion
of Georgia.

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:16.910
That’s why the New York Times asked him specifically
about the Baltic states: Estonia, Latvia,

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:18.000
and Lithuania.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.321
Russia is getting increasingly aggressive
on its boarders, and if it seems like

00:03:21.321 --> 00:03:25.100
the United States is wavering, Putin might
be more tempted to attack one of the Baltic

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.480
states as a part of a plot to destroy NATO.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:30.130
And the Republican presidential candidate
has just invited him to try.

